 </a>
 </div>
 
 <div class="cs-sticky-header">
 <div class="cs-sticky-inner">
 <img class="cs-hdr-logo" src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0722/0903/9525/files/1769431998534_Product_name.webp" alt="Nurovita">
 <a class="cs-hdr-cta" href="#nv-best-offer" data-scroll-bound="1">
 CLAIM MY DISCOUNT &nbsp;→
 </a>
 </div>
 </div>
 
 <section class="cs-dr-intro" aria-label="Crepey skin discovery intro">
 <div class="cs-dr-wrap">
 <h2 class="cs-dr-headline">
 This Clinical Discovery Helps Women Over 50 Smooth Crepey Skin In
 Weeks — Without Another Cream or 'Magic' Oil
 </h2>
 <div class="cs-dr-proof-row" aria-label="Real results">
 <img class="cs-dr-proof-img" src="https://assets.checkoutchamp.com/8c9e1110-8218-11ef-a556-ffaacc6dbefa/1782482649772_1_2_.webp" alt="Dermatologist clinical discovery for crepey skin">
 <p class="cs-dr-support">
 This breakthrough helps tighten away crepiness, support natural
 collagen production, and maintain youthful-looking skin — easier
 than ever before
 </p>
 </div>
 <div class="cs-dr-body">
 
 <div class="cs-dr-intro-copy">
 <div class="cs-dr-copy">
 <p>Skincare has never been more advanced than it is right now.</p>
 <p>So why are so many of us watching our arms, thighs, and hands turn thin and crepey — no matter how well we take care of ourselves?</p>
 <p>It's like the day you hit 50, your skin just stops bouncing back. The skin starts to crinkle and sag. It bruises at the lightest bump.</p>
 <p>The real reason has nothing to do with your genes, your skin type, or your age. Your collagen cells didn't die — they got starved.</p>
 <p class="cs-dr-strong">It's all because a single factor in your skin's protective layer has collapsed.</p>
 </div>
 </div>
 
 <div class="cs-dr-footer-band">
 <div class="cs-dr-footer-band-inner">
 <h3 class="cs-dr-emphasis">It's Not Just Aging. Experts Call It "Collagen Starvation."</h3>
 <figure class="cs-dr-collagen-fig" aria-label="Collagen starvation skin comparison">
 <img class="cs-dr-collagen-img" src="https://assets.checkoutchamp.com/8c9e1110-8218-11ef-a556-ffaacc6dbefa/1782482679174_3_1_.webp" alt="Collagen starvation skin comparison">
 </figure>
 <div class="cs-dr-copy cs-dr-collagen-copy">
 <p>Did your skin look fine in your 40s — then almost the second menopause hit, it turned thin, crinkly, and bruised at the lightest bump?</p>
 <p>You're not crazy, and it's not "just aging."</p>
 <p><strong>When estrogen drops at menopause, your skin stops getting the signal to build collagen — so your collagen slowly starves.</strong></p>
 <p>That collagen was the cushion that kept your skin firm and packed tight from underneath.</p>
 <p>Without that cushion, the surface loses its support and starts to sink.</p>
 <p>Your skin turns as thin as tissue paper, one small bump on the coffee table now blooms into a dark, purple bruise.</p>
 <p><strong>That's why every drugstore lotion and pricey body oil has failed you: none of them ever reached the deep layer underneath, where the real problem lives.</strong></p>
 </div>
 <figure class="cs-dr-surface-fail-fig" aria-label="Surface creams cannot reach collagen layer">
 <img class="cs-dr-collagen-img" src="https://assets.checkoutchamp.com/8c9e1110-8218-11ef-a556-ffaacc6dbefa/1782482770095_5_1_.webp" alt="Surface creams and oils cannot reach collagen starvation layer">
 </figure>
 </div>
 </div>
 
 <div class="cs-dr-added-band">
 <h3 class="cs-dr-emphasis">Creams and Oils Stop at the Surface. Supplements Just Get Digested — So Where's the Real Problem?</h3>
 <figure class="cs-dr-stacked-fig" aria-label="How the roller reaches the starving layer">
 <video class="cs-dr-stacked-video" autoplay="" muted="" loop="" playsinline="" preload="metadata" src="https://cdn.shopify.com/videos/c/o/v/3777726cdc4744878465a896cba29d29.mp4"></video>
 </figure>
 <div class="cs-dr-copy">
 <p>They just smear heavy grease across the dead surface of your skin. They do absolutely nothing to wake the sleeping, starved cells buried underneath.</p>
 <p>The problem lives underneath — deeper than you'd ever guess. The cells that build your collagen sit three layers down. A night cream never reaches them.</p>
 <p>So night after night, you fed the very top of your skin. Meanwhile the one layer that actually needed it kept starving in the dark.</p>
 <p>That's why your skin kept thinning, no matter what you tried. It was never that you didn't try hard enough. You aimed at the wrong layer.</p>
 <p><strong>You cannot fix Collagen Starvation by moisturizing the surface.</strong></p>
 <p>But what if you could wake those starved cells without waiting on your hormones — and force them to rebuild the cushion your skin is missing?</p>
 </div>
 </div>
 
 <div class="cs-dr-added-band">
 <h3 class="cs-dr-emphasis">So We Built One Simple Roll to Finally Reach the Layer That's Starving.</h3>
 <figure class="cs-dr-stacked-fig" aria-label="Natural Cooling Roller product">
 <img class="cs-dr-collagen-img" src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0722/0903/9525/files/productt.webp" alt="Natural Cooling Roller product">
 </figure>
 <div class="cs-dr-copy">
 <p>It's built on a 100% natural botanical formula, with clinical concentrations inspired by years of work inside Europe's health clinics.</p>
 <p>Greasy formulas just sit on top and never move. This one is a roller, so you massage the deep ingredients down where they belong — and it sinks in.</p>
 <p><strong>Inside is clinical-grade 8% Centella, in a penetrating formula that can ACTUALLY stimulate your collagen — not just coat the surface like an expensive moisturizer.</strong></p>
 <p>One roll-on. About 30 seconds. It carries what your starved cells have waited for past the surface — and that cool wave? That's how you know it's reaching them.</p>
 </div>
 </div>
 </div>
 </div>
 </section>
</div>
<script>
(function(){
 var banner = document.querySelector('.cs-banner');
 var hdr = document.querySelector('.cs-sticky-header');
 if (!hdr || !banner) return;
 /* Placeholder keeps the space in the layout when header turns fixed */
 var placeholder = document.createElement('div');
 var isFixed = false;
 function makeFixed() {
 if (isFixed) return;
 isFixed = true;
 placeholder.style.height = hdr.offsetHeight + 'px';
 placeholder.style.display = 'block';
 hdr.parentNode.insertBefore(placeholder, hdr);
 hdr.classList.add('cs-hdr-fixed');
 document.body.appendChild(hdr);
 }
 function makeNormal() {
 if (!isFixed) return;
 isFixed = false;
 hdr.classList.remove('cs-hdr-fixed');
 placeholder.parentNode && placeholder.parentNode.insertBefore(hdr, placeholder.nextSibling);
 placeholder.parentNode && placeholder.parentNode.removeChild(placeholder);
 }
 function onScroll() {
 if (window.pageYOffset >= 100) {
 makeFixed();
 } else {
 makeNormal();
 }
 }
 window.addEventListener('scroll', onScroll, { passive: true });
 onScroll();
 /* ── CTA scroll-to-offer ── */
 document.querySelectorAll('a[href="#nv-best-offer"]').forEach(function(link) {
 if (link.dataset.scrollBound) return;
 link.dataset.scrollBound = '1';
 link.addEventListener('click', function(e) {
 var isMobile = window.innerWidth < 768;
 var target = isMobile
 ? (document.querySelector('kaching-bundles-block') ||
 document.getElementById('nv-best-offer'))
 : document.getElementById('nv-best-offer');
 if (target) {
 e.preventDefault();
 var offset = hdr ? hdr.offsetHeight : 0;
 var top = target.getBoundingClientRect().top + window.pageYOffset - offset;
 window.scrollTo({ top: top, behavior: 'smooth' });
 }
 });
 });
})();
</script>
